# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working
# tree, on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: this machine has core.autocrlf=true, so git
# rewrote LF to CRLF on checkout while build-guides.py writes LF. A
# clean clone followed by a regeneration therefore showed all five
# guides as modified when nothing had actually changed. A daily cloud
# routine would have buried its real diff in that noise on every run.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for these paths, so the Linux cloud runner
# and this Windows machine produce byte-identical output.

*           text=auto eol=lf

*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
